/* book Worked example: Q: An aircraft cruises at 35 000 ft, where the ambient pressure is 23.8 kPa. The cabin is held at 8000 ft, where the pressure is 75.3 kPa. (a) Find the differential pressure in kPa and in psi. (b) Find the outward force on a plug-type door of area 1.2 m². Take 1 psi = 6.895 kPa.
   1. List the data: p_cabin = 75.3 kPa, p_ambient = 23.8 kPa, A = 1.2 m².
   2. Differential pressure: Δp = 75.3 − 23.8 = 51.5 kPa.
   3. In psi: 51.5 ÷ 6.895 = 7.47 psi.
   4. Convert to base units: 51.5 kPa = 51 500 Pa.
   5. Force: F = Δp × A = 51 500 × 1.2 = 61 800 N = 61.8 kN.
   Answer: Differential pressure 51.5 kPa (7.47 psi); outward force on the door 61.8 kN. */
