/* book exam traps: Saying the pack compressor cools the air. It heats it. The turbine cools it, because the air gives up shaft work there. | Saying the supply pressure sets the cabin pressure. The outflow valve sets it; the supply only has to cover the leak plus the outflow. | Mixing cabin altitude with aircraft altitude: the cabin is at 8000 ft while the aircraft is at 35 000 ft. | Unit slips in Δp × A: kPa must become Pa (× 1000) before multiplying by area in m², or the force comes out 1000 times too small; and the turbine formula needs kelvin, not °C. | Reversing the relief valves. The positive relief valve opens outward on excess Δp; the negative relief valve opens inward when outside pressure wins. */
