/* book exam traps: Swapping condenser and evaporator. The condenser is the hot one that rejects heat outside; the evaporator is the cold one inside the cabin duct. | Thinking COP above 1 breaks the first law. It does not: the extra heat at the condenser is the compressor work, and Qcond = Qevap + Wcomp always holds. | Using condenser heat in the COP. COP is Qevap ÷ Wcomp, never Qcond ÷ Wcomp. | Forgetting that the expansion valve does no work. It only drops pressure and temperature; the compressor is the only work input. | Treating the vapour cycle as an open system like the air cycle machine. It is closed: the same refrigerant charge circulates again and again. */
